[2026-03-15T20:22:23.308Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ETZ5KMo5vkRScKcqXeNR2B","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Test Instructions\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here are the key steps for recording with Replay CLI:\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\n1. **Install**: `npm i -g replayio` (or use yarn/pnpm/bun)\n\n2. **Authenticate**: Set your `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable from https://app.replay.io settings\n\n3. **Record a Session**: \n   - Run `replayio record https://myapp.com` to launch the browser and begin capturing\n   - The recording continues until you close the browser\n\n4. **Upload**: \n   - Use `replayio upload <recording-id>` to upload your captured session\n   - This provides a shareable URL for viewing the recording\n\n## Key Commands\n\nThe documentation covers commands like `list` (view recordings), `remove` (delete recordings), and `upload-source-maps` (for source map management), but **does not include specific instructions for running automated tests** with Replay CLI.\n\nThe reference material focuses on interactive recording workflows rather than test automation scenarios. For test integration guidance, you'd need additional documentation beyond what's provided here."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7578dc23-09a2-46c9-ace4-1453e464055f","uuid":"a876aad9-5b15-4282-9171-9ad91f795818","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Test Instructions\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here are the key steps for recording with Replay CLI:\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\n1. **Install**: `npm i -g replayio` (or use yarn/pnpm/bun)\n\n2. **Authenticate**: Set your `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable from https://app.replay.io settings\n\n3. **Record a Session**: \n   - Run `replayio record https://myapp.com` to launch the browser and begin capturing\n   - The recording continues until you close the browser\n\n4. **Upload**: \n   - Use `replayio upload <recording-id>` to upload your captured session\n   - This provides a shareable URL for viewing the recording\n\n## Key Commands\n\nThe documentation covers commands like `list` (view recordings), `remove` (delete recordings), and `upload-source-maps` (for source map management), but **does not include specific instructions for running automated tests** with Replay CLI.\n\nThe reference material focuses on interactive recording workflows rather than test automation scenarios. For test integration guidance, you'd need additional documentation beyond what's provided here.","durationMs":3558,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T20:22:23.574Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013dQJ4Xn1G4c3tk2h3zePkJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Key Instructions for Using Replay MCP for Debugging\n\n## Investigation Framework\n\nFollow this structured approach when investigating recordings:\n\n1. **Formulate a Question**: Frame your debugging task as a specific question about app behavior\n2. **Explore**: Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events in the recording\n3. **Explain**: Apply explanatory tools to understand *why* those events occurred\n4. **Hypothesis**: Form a conclusion supported by gathered data\n5. **Document**: Reference the data that justifies your findings\n\n## Essential Strategies\n\n**For Code-Related Issues**:\nThe guidance suggests to \"find code relevant to the question being answered, see whether that code executed at all, and get details about the times when it executed.\" The Logpoint tool is particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution points.\n\n**For Timing Problems**:\nLocate the relevant event point and use ControlDependency to \"explore the events that had to happen first and any associated delays.\"\n\n## Critical Mindset\n\nAvoid jumping to conclusions. Instead, use the recording as a \"gigantic database\" where every executed statement creates a detectable point, allowing precise investigation of app behavior without assumptions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7578dc23-09a2-46c9-ace4-1453e464055f","uuid":"0c5c15fd-6e16-4432-99bf-bfbfe293017a","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Key Instructions for Using Replay MCP for Debugging\n\n## Investigation Framework\n\nFollow this structured approach when investigating recordings:\n\n1. **Formulate a Question**: Frame your debugging task as a specific question about app behavior\n2. **Explore**: Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events in the recording\n3. **Explain**: Apply explanatory tools to understand *why* those events occurred\n4. **Hypothesis**: Form a conclusion supported by gathered data\n5. **Document**: Reference the data that justifies your findings\n\n## Essential Strategies\n\n**For Code-Related Issues**:\nThe guidance suggests to \"find code relevant to the question being answered, see whether that code executed at all, and get details about the times when it executed.\" The Logpoint tool is particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution points.\n\n**For Timing Problems**:\nLocate the relevant event point and use ControlDependency to \"explore the events that had to happen first and any associated delays.\"\n\n## Critical Mindset\n\nAvoid jumping to conclusions. Instead, use the recording as a \"gigantic database\" where every executed statement creates a detectable point, allowing precise investigation of app behavior without assumptions.","durationMs":3071,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
